<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan to tender for 72,000 tonnes U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>Taiwan to tender for 72,000 tonnes U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Taiwan Flour Mills Association will place a tender on Wednesday for two shipments totalling 72,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat, traders said on Monday.  </p>
<p>Both shipments would be specified for delivery from the Pacific Northwest, traders said. Other shipping specifications were not yet available, they said.</p>
<p>The milling association is placing the tender on behalf of several major Taiwan wheat buying companies, chiefly President Enterprise, Tai Yu Products, Chia Hsin, Formosa Oilseed and Lien Hwa Industry as well as other wheat millers.  </p>
<p>Details for the tender are as follow:</p>
<p> Type			Tonnage    Delivery Date</p>
<p>Shipment One</p>
<p>					    Dec 15- Jan 5</p>
<p> Dark Northern Spring  16,600</p>
<p> Hard Red Winter	 10,700</p>
<p> White Wheat		6,700</p>
<p>Shipment Two</p>
<p>					    Dec 30- Jan 20</p>
<p> Dark Northern Spring  22,400</p>
<p> Hard Red Winter	  9,400</p>
<p> White Wheat		6,200</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
